#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:7
msgid ""
"Threads are a key part of the messaging experience in Mattermost. They're"
" used to organize conversations and enable users to discuss topics "
"without adding noise to channels or direct messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:9
msgid ""
"Threaded discussions offers an enhanced experience for users "
"communicating in threads and replying to messages that includes a unified"
" threads inbox to read all conversations in one view. Threads improve the"
" ability to process channel content, find, follow, and resume "
"conversations more easily, and keep threaded conversations focused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:11
msgid "Organize conversations using threaded discussions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:16
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v7.0, threaded discussions are enabled by default for all"
" new Mattermost deployments. All Mattermost users can create new threads,"
" unless the system admin has :ref:`disabled the ability to do so "
"<administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings:threaded "
"discussions>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:17
msgid ""
"System admins can :ref:`configure default availability and user opt-in "
"<administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings:threaded "
"discussions>` of threaded discussions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:20
msgid "Start or reply to threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:22
msgid ""
":doc:`Replies to messages </end-user-guide/collaborate/reply-to-"
"messages>` are collapsed under the first message of a thread. Open a "
"thread by selecting the message or reply count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:24
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11.2, when using Mattermost in a web browser, you can "
"open threads in separate browser windows by selecting the **New Window** "
"|new-window-icon| icon in the thread header. This allows you to view and "
"participate in multiple threads simultaneously without losing context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:146
msgid "Open thread in a new browser window icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:27
msgid "Follow threads and messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:29
msgid ""
"You'll automatically follow every thread you participate or are mentioned"
" in. You can manually follow particular messages and threads so that any "
"reply activity triggers :doc:`notifications </end-user-guide/preferences"
"/manage-your-notifications>`. Follow or unfollow any thread, at any time."
" In channels, a dot next to thread participants means there are unread "
"replies for the threads you're following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:31
msgid "Follow threads to stay updated on replies to messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:36
msgid ""
"Toggle the thread’s **Follow** option, or select **Follow thread** from "
"the **More Actions** |more-icon| icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:16
msgid "Use the More icon to access additional message options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:38
#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:75
msgid "Unfollow threads from the More Actions icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:42
msgid ""
"Follow messages with no replies from the **More Actions** |more-icon| "
"icon to be notified if someone replies to the message later based on your"
" notification preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:43
msgid ""
"You can also use keyboard arrow keys to navigate threads in the "
"**Threads** view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:47
msgid ""
"Long-press on a message to access message options, then tap **Follow "
"Thread**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:49
msgid "Tap and hold on a message thread to select Follow Thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:53
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also tap on the **Follow** indicator below a "
"message thread to follow it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:55
msgid "Toggle the Follow indicator to start folowing a thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:60
msgid ""
"Follow messages with no replies from the **More Actions** |more-icon-"
"vertical| icon to be notified if someone replies to the message later "
"based on your notification preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:50
msgid ""
"Use the More icon in the top left corner to access Mattermost desktop "
"apps customization settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:62
msgid "Tap and hold on a message with no replies to select Follow Message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:67
msgid "Unfollow threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:69
msgid ""
"If you’re no longer interested in a or message thread, unfollow it to "
"stop receiving notifications. Viewing a thread without responding to it "
"doesn’t automatically follow that thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:73
msgid ""
"Toggle the thread’s **Following** indicator, or select **Unfollow "
"thread** from the **More Actions** |more-icon| icon to unfollow it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:80
msgid ""
"Long-press on a message to access message options, then tap **Unfollow "
"Thread**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:82
msgid ""
"Tap and hold on a message thread you're following to select Unfollow "
"Thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:86
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can tap on the **Following** indicator below the "
"message thread to unfollow it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:88
msgid "Toggle the Following indicator to stop following a thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:93
msgid "View all threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:95
msgid ""
"Select **Threads** at the top of the channel sidebar to see all your "
"followed threads on the currently selected team. Threads with the most "
"recent replies display at the top of the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:97
msgid ""
"Select **Unreads** to filter your followed threads by only those with "
"unread replies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations.rst:99
msgid ""
"Select Threads in the channel sidebar to see all thread updates in your "
"Threads View."
msgstr ""

